Cell["\<\
The gain jumped from ~2 dBi to ~9\[Dash]10 dBi, and the front-to-back ratio \
tells us the beam is ~15\[Dash]20 dB stronger forward than backward. We \
didn't add any power \[LongDash] we redistributed it by controlling the \
currents on the parasitic elements. Try nudging the director lengths or \
spacings and re-running: you are now doing real antenna design.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200875759659*^9},
 CellID->999853030,ExpressionUUID->"bec9a5a9-acb3-413a-befc-22ecebf369f4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Antennas Over Ground: The Monopole", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, {3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200898334832*^9}},
 CellID->1935290158,ExpressionUUID->"b2edf066-eec9-464e-8d9f-8a25aff4c7b0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Real antennas sit above the earth, which reflects radio waves. A beautiful \
shortcut called image theory says a perfect conducting ground behaves exactly \
as if there were a mirror-image antenna underneath. So a quarter-wave \
monopole standing on a ground plane behaves like the top half of a half-wave \
dipole \[LongDash] the ground \"supplies\" the missing bottom half:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200917184598*^9},
 CellID->1603702598,ExpressionUUID->"8e3617d1-b4b3-47ec-93b0-e5c08ab77c9f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"monopole", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<Segments\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "11"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Tag\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<P1\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<P2\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0.25"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Radius\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "0.001"}]}], "|>"}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, {3.990200918949441*^9, 
   3.990200928002161*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[200]:=",
 CellID->1396458170,ExpressionUUID->"c2c48982-0a78-4240-9610-70ca9ea3a8a7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"feed", "     ", "=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<Tag\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Segment\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<Voltage\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1.0"}]}], "|>"}], "}"}]}], 
   ";"}], " "}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, {3.990200918949441*^9, 
   3.9902009425409613`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[201]:=",
 CellID->84794551,ExpressionUUID->"0f330b81-6803-4f76-8a71-de4ecc861825"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AntennaSolveMemory", "[", 
    RowBox[{"monopole", ",", " ", "300.0", ",", " ", "feed", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Ground\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"<|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<Type\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Perfect\>\""}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<ConnectWires\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]}], 
       "|>"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, {3.990200918949441*^9, 
   3.990200935598509*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[202]:=",
 CellID->1468611004,ExpressionUUID->"32e143b2-7078-4d3b-8451-9e84f5a1e55f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"sol", "[", "\"\<InputParameters\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "\"\<ZInput\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, {3.990200918949441*^9, 
   3.990200938597002*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[203]:=",
 CellID->1915589257,ExpressionUUID->"4cb50d80-63a4-41bf-a3cd-a5a673532a36"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"42.136108770237854`", "\[VeryThinSpace]", "+", 
  RowBox[{"24.78691735517558`", " ", "\[ImaginaryI]"}]}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.990200946468052*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[203]=",
 CellID->761171502,ExpressionUUID->"98493df6-0d45-426f-a900-de65a0388213"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Notice the impedance is roughly half that of the dipole (~",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"73", " ", "\[CapitalOmega]"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineMath",
  ExpressionUUID->"02a39abb-988b-4c6d-8378-e019e3ab8374"],
 " \[RightArrow] ~",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"36", " ", "\[CapitalOmega]"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineMath",
  ExpressionUUID->"ec9074f3-46be-4451-bceb-c4616d6190ad"],
 " at resonance). That is image theory in action: the monopole radiates into \
only the upper half-space, so for the same current it sends out half the \
power, and ",
 StyleBox["Z\[LongEqual]V/I",
  Deletable->True],
 " halves. The radiation pattern is correspondingly the top half of the \
dipole doughnut. Monopoles are everywhere \[LongDash] car radios, cell \
towers, the \"rubber duck\" on a walkie-talkie \[LongDash] precisely because \
they are half the size of a dipole and use the ground as their other half.\n\
Try ",
 StyleBox["\"Type\"->\"Realistic\"", "InlineCode"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["\"Dielectric\"", "InlineCode"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["\"Conductivity\"", "InlineCode"],
 " values to see how real, lossy earth (instead of a perfect mirror) changes \
the impedance and pattern."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200918949441*^9, {
   3.990200975844902*^9, 3.99020098406253*^9}, {3.990201038447721*^9, 
   3.990201057577043*^9}},
 CellID->1019488835,ExpressionUUID->"bed8aa1b-611d-4a15-9e14-c213854bffc5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Where To Go From Here", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200918949441*^9, {
   3.990200975844902*^9, 3.99020098406253*^9}, {3.990201038447721*^9, 
   3.9902010780004997`*^9}},
 CellID->176714023,ExpressionUUID->"d3f0cfcd-a81c-43ba-807c-3f145d38b514"],

Cell["\<\
You now have the core ideas: current distribution \[RightArrow] impedance \
\[RightArrow] radiation pattern \[RightArrow] directivity, plus matching, \
polarization, parasitic directivity, and ground effects. Everything else in \
antennas builds on these. Good next experiments with AntennaLink:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200918949441*^9, {
   3.990200975844902*^9, 3.99020098406253*^9}, {3.990201038447721*^9, 
   3.9902010615069427`*^9}, {3.990201101705863*^9, 3.990201110183202*^9}},
 CellID->612667447,ExpressionUUID->"82d8dedc-b0e0-4e12-9b02-93ea1ad306c6"],

Cell["\<\
Short antennas and loading. Make the dipole 0.3 m (too short to resonate), \
watch the huge capacitive reactance, then cancel it with a center loading \
coil using the \"Loads\" option. See README Example 4.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200918949441*^9, {
   3.990200975844902*^9, 3.99020098406253*^9}, {3.990201038447721*^9, 
   3.9902010615069427`*^9}, {3.990201101705863*^9, 3.990201141170227*^9}},
 CellID->1966091591,ExpressionUUID->"0346e91c-4cc5-4f87-bf37-cb1335bf1dd1"],

Cell["\<\
Circular polarization. Build a helix and compute its axial ratio from \
ETheta/EPhi. See README Example 5.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200918949441*^9, {
   3.990200975844902*^9, 3.99020098406253*^9}, {3.990201038447721*^9, 
   3.9902010615069427`*^9}, {3.990201101705863*^9, 3.990201143819976*^9}},
 CellID->770493548,ExpressionUUID->"edba452f-0f56-4b90-84b1-3fa6d9bbab47"],

Cell["\<\
Bigger arrays. Add more directors to the Yagi and watch gain climb (with \
diminishing returns). Sweep an element spacing and plot gain vs spacing.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200918949441*^9, {
   3.990200975844902*^9, 3.99020098406253*^9}, {3.990201038447721*^9, 
   3.9902010615069427`*^9}, {3.990201101705863*^9, 3.9902011465862093`*^9}},
 CellID->358669826,ExpressionUUID->"230aa159-83a0-4c87-bbc2-50e48abd1d8d"],

Cell["\<\
A full worked design. The runnable examples/DishAntenna.wl builds a fed \
parabolic reflector and visualizes everything end to end.\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200918949441*^9, {
   3.990200975844902*^9, 3.99020098406253*^9}, {3.990201038447721*^9, 
   3.9902010615069427`*^9}, {3.990201101705863*^9, 3.990201121167262*^9}, 
   3.990201151556088*^9},
 CellID->177168453,ExpressionUUID->"bd8cf874-ec00-40a8-91a9-dc2fc5195603"],

Cell["\<\
Change the numbers, break things, and watch the patterns move \[LongDash] \
that is the fastest way to build antenna intuition.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.990200541943589*^9, 3.990200584043126*^9, {3.990200664527944*^9, 
   3.990200670231249*^9}, 3.990200877519143*^9, 3.990200918949441*^9, {
   3.990200975844902*^9, 3.99020098406253*^9}, {3.990201038447721*^9, 
   3.9902010615069427`*^9}, 3.990201101705863*^9},
 CellID->1257854829,ExpressionUUID->"29477ff0-95c0-4688-9e3a-39a03a628bab"]
}, Open  ]],

